277
00:11:46,719 --> 00:11:48,859
Heh. Oops.

278
00:11:48,863 --> 00:11:51,363
Somebody around here needs a bath.

279
00:11:51,363 --> 00:11:52,363
Yep, me.

280
00:11:52,363 --> 00:11:56,363
Oh, if I'm going to take a bath, then I'm going to need...

281
00:11:57,363 --> 00:11:58,843
a big bottle of water.

282
00:11:58,847 --> 00:12:00,187
Bubble bath!

283
00:12:02,887 --> 00:12:03,887
Ah.

284
00:12:04,987 --> 00:12:07,147
If you give a mouse a bottle of bubble bath,

285
00:12:07,527 --> 00:12:08,827
then he's going to say...

286
00:12:08,831 --> 00:12:12,331
Wait, I really, really need...

287
00:12:12,331 --> 00:12:15,331
Exactly, my toy boat.

288
00:12:15,331 --> 00:12:18,811
Hark all ye mateys, Captain Mouse's boat.

289
00:12:18,815 --> 00:12:20,895
heading out to the seven seas.

290
00:12:20,975 --> 00:12:22,855
Aye-aye, Captain Mouse.

291
00:12:22,935 --> 00:12:24,355
Oh, Oliver!

292
00:12:24,435 --> 00:12:26,115
You know what else I need?

293
00:12:26,195 --> 00:12:27,195
This way.

294
00:12:27,275 --> 00:12:28,795
If your mouse is a sea captain,

295
00:12:28,799 --> 00:12:30,799
Then I'll probably want...

296
00:12:33,799 --> 00:12:35,099
A captain's hat!

297
00:12:35,199 --> 00:12:37,599
Uh, that's more of a sombrero.

298
00:12:37,699 --> 00:12:38,779
Oh, right.

299
00:12:38,783 --> 00:12:40,783
Ha! My captain's hat!

300
00:12:40,783 --> 00:12:42,783
Looking good there.

301
00:12:42,783 --> 00:12:44,783
Really?

302
00:12:46,783 --> 00:12:48,763
Ugh!

303
00:12:48,767 --> 00:12:51,107
And when you're a daring sea captain,

304
00:12:51,107 --> 00:12:53,727
then you want to go on a big adventure

305
00:12:53,727 --> 00:12:57,947
and discover somewhere new, uncharted territory.

306
00:12:57,947 --> 00:12:58,747
Ready, Oliver?

307
00:12:58,751 --> 00:13:01,251
- Sounds great, but I've got school.

308
00:13:01,251 --> 00:13:02,331
- Oh.

309
00:13:02,331 --> 00:13:04,791
- You go and tell me all about it when I get home.

310
00:13:04,791 --> 00:13:06,851
- Okay, but I'll miss you.

311
00:13:06,851 --> 00:13:08,731
Have a good day.

312
00:13:08,735 --> 00:13:12,735
What else does a daring captain need for a sea voyage?

313
00:13:12,735 --> 00:13:14,735
Pants!

314
00:13:14,735 --> 00:13:18,715
Oh, right.

315
00:13:18,719 --> 00:13:22,059
Huh? Hmm.

316
00:13:22,059 --> 00:13:25,519
If I'm going to go on a daring adventure, then...

317
00:13:25,519 --> 00:13:28,699
I'll need a bigger boat!

318
00:13:28,703 --> 00:13:34,903
Where is it?

319
00:13:34,903 --> 00:13:36,123
Where is it?

320
00:13:38,687 --> 00:13:40,527
Aha! My boat!

321
00:13:40,527 --> 00:13:42,727
Which needs a whole lot of air.

322
00:13:42,727 --> 00:13:43,987
No problem.

323
00:13:43,987 --> 00:13:47,067
Step one, attach foot pump to the air nozzle.

324
00:13:47,067 --> 00:13:48,667
Step two, pump the air.

325
00:13:48,671 --> 00:13:49,871
in air.

326
00:13:49,871 --> 00:13:50,871
Easy peasy.

327
00:13:56,571 --> 00:13:58,651
A little more

328
00:13:58,655 --> 00:14:00,655
Easy. Then, easy.

329
00:14:00,655 --> 00:14:02,655
Oh.

330
00:14:06,655 --> 00:14:08,635
Something tells me I'm not going to do this.

331
00:14:08,639 --> 00:14:10,639
there's a story to that.

332
00:14:10,639 --> 00:14:11,979
Ooh, okay.

333
00:14:11,979 --> 00:14:13,979
That was harder than it looked.

334
00:14:13,979 --> 00:14:15,479
Cat, hello!

335
00:14:15,479 --> 00:14:16,639
You're just in time.

336
00:14:16,639 --> 00:14:17,639
Hello, Mouse.

337
00:14:17,639 --> 00:14:18,619
In time for walking.

338
00:14:18,623 --> 00:14:20,383
I'm getting ready to sail off.

339
00:14:20,383 --> 00:14:21,923
Will you join my crew?

340
00:14:21,923 --> 00:14:23,923
Intriguing offer.

341
00:14:23,923 --> 00:14:25,623
I love boats.

342
00:14:25,623 --> 00:14:28,603
Sailboats, motorboats, tugboats.

343
00:14:28,607 --> 00:14:30,107
Hmm, where's yours?

344
00:14:30,407 --> 00:14:32,347
Glad you asked. My boat.

345
00:14:32,827 --> 00:14:35,367
You mean the boat that doesn't have any air in it?

346
00:14:35,527 --> 00:14:36,747
That's where you come in.

347
00:14:38,591 --> 00:14:43,951
Little more! We're almost there!

348
00:14:44,271 --> 00:14:46,831
I suspect we're... there!

349
00:14:47,391 --> 00:14:48,071
All right!

350
00:14:48,575 --> 00:14:51,695
Well done!

351
00:14:51,695 --> 00:14:55,535
Uh, how are we gonna get this expertly inflated boat in the water?

352
00:14:55,535 --> 00:14:57,535
Hmm.

353
00:14:57,535 --> 00:14:58,555
Idea!

354
00:14:58,559 --> 00:15:00,439
Follow me! We'll need Pig's help!

355
00:15:01,779 --> 00:15:02,999
Are you guys ready?

356
00:15:03,339 --> 00:15:05,139
All tied up and ready to go!

357
00:15:08,543 --> 00:15:12,543
Oh, look! We're almost at the lake! Good job, Pig!

358
00:15:12,543 --> 00:15:18,523
Thanks, Mouse. Or should I say, "Aye-aye, Captain Mouse!"

359
00:15:18,527 --> 00:15:20,527
I get the sound of that.

360
00:15:20,527 --> 00:15:22,527
We made it!

361
00:15:22,527 --> 00:15:24,527
What's in here?

362
00:15:24,527 --> 00:15:26,527
I personalised our life jackets.

363
00:15:26,527 --> 00:15:28,507
See? This one is too big.

364
00:15:28,511 --> 00:15:30,511
This one is for mouse, this one is for pig,

365
00:15:30,511 --> 00:15:32,511
and this one is for cat.

366
00:15:35,511 --> 00:15:38,491
And I had a little extra time left over to make it.

367
00:15:38,495 --> 00:15:41,535
- We'll make these sparkle oars.

368
00:15:41,535 --> 00:15:42,695
- Remarkable.

369
00:15:44,135 --> 00:15:45,135
- And what's this?

370
00:15:45,135 --> 00:15:46,975
- Oh, our picnic lunch.

371
00:15:46,975 --> 00:15:48,475
You can't set out to see without

372
00:15:48,479 --> 00:15:49,479
Provisions?

373
00:15:49,479 --> 00:15:50,479
Provisions?

374
00:15:50,479 --> 00:15:52,479
Does that include cookies?

375
00:15:52,479 --> 00:15:53,479
You'll see.

376
00:15:53,479 --> 00:15:55,479
Let's get the boat in the water.

377
00:15:55,479 --> 00:15:58,459
Good idea.

378
00:15:58,463 --> 00:16:00,463
Oh no! Wait for me!

379
00:16:05,463 --> 00:16:08,443
Phew! Made it!

380
00:16:08,447 --> 00:16:18,427
Stroke! Stroke! And one! And two! And one! Two! One! Two! Three!

381
00:16:18,431 --> 00:16:21,811
-

382
00:16:21,811 --> 00:16:24,231
-Excuse me. Sorry. Oh, pardon me. Uh-oh.

383
00:16:24,231 --> 00:16:25,811
-See? Oh! -

384
00:16:25,811 --> 00:16:28,411
Sorry. If I start counting, then I just...

385
00:16:28,415 --> 00:16:30,255
- Have to dance. - No worries.

386
00:16:32,035 --> 00:16:33,035
Oh, look!

387
00:16:33,375 --> 00:16:35,715
Hi, Moose! It's us!

388
00:16:35,915 --> 00:16:38,395
Hi, Moose! Moose! Moose, we're here!

389
00:16:38,399 --> 00:16:39,399
Over here!

390
00:16:39,399 --> 00:16:40,399
See?

391
00:16:40,399 --> 00:16:41,399
Here?

392
00:16:41,399 --> 00:16:42,399
Whoa!

393
00:16:42,399 --> 00:16:45,399
I have to stop doing that.

394
00:16:45,399 --> 00:16:46,399
Hi, pig!

395
00:16:46,399 --> 00:16:47,399
Hi, cat!

396
00:16:47,399 --> 00:16:48,379
Hi, mouse!

397
00:16:48,383 --> 00:16:49,423
- Where are you going?

398
00:16:49,423 --> 00:16:52,483
- Somewhere new, uncharted territory.

399
00:16:52,483 --> 00:16:53,823
Big boat adventure.

400
00:16:53,823 --> 00:16:58,363
- Wow, good luck, bon voyage.

401
00:16:58,367 --> 00:17:00,367
Land ahoy!

402
00:17:00,367 --> 00:17:02,367
This is what we've been looking for.

403
00:17:02,367 --> 00:17:04,367
Uncharted territory.

404
00:17:04,367 --> 00:17:06,367
And if you see uncharted territory,

405
00:17:06,367 --> 00:17:08,347
we'll be able to find the way to find the way.

406
00:17:08,351 --> 00:17:12,691
- Uncharted territory, then there's only one thing to do.

407
00:17:12,691 --> 00:17:13,771
- Explore it.

408
00:17:16,691 --> 00:17:18,331
- Prepare to land.

409
00:17:18,335 --> 00:17:19,995
- Aye, aye, Captain!

410
00:17:19,995 --> 00:17:22,415
- Tie the boat to the tree, then it won't float away.

411
00:17:22,415 --> 00:17:23,875
- Aye, aye, Captain!

412
00:17:23,875 --> 00:17:25,835
- Our island awaits.

413
00:17:26,835 --> 00:17:28,315
- Oh, wait!

414
00:17:28,319 --> 00:17:29,819
I almost forgot.

415
00:17:29,819 --> 00:17:31,319
Now I'm ready.

416
00:17:31,319 --> 00:17:32,239
Time to explore.

417
00:17:38,303 --> 00:17:43,303
Just think, we're the first ones to find the way here.

418
00:17:43,303 --> 00:17:47,303
What an adventure!

419
00:17:47,303 --> 00:17:48,283
Oh, my gosh.

420
00:17:48,287 --> 00:17:50,287
Where to next?

421
00:17:50,287 --> 00:17:54,287
The tippy top of that mountain.

422
00:17:54,287 --> 00:17:58,267
Come on!

423
00:17:58,271 --> 00:18:02,111
We did it!

424
00:18:02,111 --> 00:18:04,611
The top of the world!

425
00:18:04,611 --> 00:18:08,251
I hereby pronounce this island discovered by...

426
00:18:08,255 --> 00:18:10,915
- At Pig! - Captain Mouse!

427
00:18:11,015 --> 00:18:14,755
And I hereby pronounce it's picnic time!

428
00:18:17,255 --> 00:18:18,235
- -

429
00:18:18,239 --> 00:18:19,699
Whoa!

430
00:18:19,699 --> 00:18:21,779
Pig, you're amazing.

431
00:18:21,779 --> 00:18:23,779
You even brought fruit smoothies.

432
00:18:23,779 --> 00:18:24,779
Mm-hmm.

433
00:18:24,779 --> 00:18:28,219
I always say everybody needs a solar-powered jet

434
00:18:28,223 --> 00:18:30,223
- I'll put a blender on a picnic.

435
00:18:30,223 --> 00:18:32,223
- Anything else in here?

436
00:18:32,223 --> 00:18:33,223
- Of course.

437
00:18:35,223 --> 00:18:36,223
- Thank you.

438
00:18:36,223 --> 00:18:38,203
Cookies.

439
00:18:38,207 --> 00:18:39,047
- Bye-bye.

440
00:18:41,047 --> 00:18:44,707
- I figured you'd need it on a daring adventure.

441
00:18:44,707 --> 00:18:48,187
- I hope Oliver's having as much fun as we are.

442
00:18:48,191 --> 00:18:51,191
Mouse? Where are you?

443
00:18:51,191 --> 00:18:52,191
Mouse?

444
00:18:54,191 --> 00:18:55,191
Mouse?

445
00:18:56,191 --> 00:18:58,171
Aha!

446
00:18:58,175 --> 00:18:59,335
- Are they back yet?

447
00:18:59,335 --> 00:19:00,635
- Doesn't look like it.

448
00:19:00,635 --> 00:19:02,175
Where'd he go to explore?

449
00:19:02,175 --> 00:19:03,715
The Atlantic Ocean?

450
00:19:03,715 --> 00:19:05,075
The Black Sea?

451
00:19:05,075 --> 00:19:06,115
- The park.

452
00:19:06,115 --> 00:19:07,055
- Ah, okay.

453
00:19:07,055 --> 00:19:08,155
I'll go find him, thanks.

454
00:19:08,159 --> 00:19:18,139
Well, time to go home. Cast your eye one last time on the grand vista.

455
00:19:18,143 --> 00:19:19,803
from our island.

456
00:19:19,803 --> 00:19:20,683
Look!

457
00:19:20,683 --> 00:19:23,103
Some unlucky captain lost his boat.

458
00:19:23,103 --> 00:19:25,483
And his sparkle oars.

459
00:19:25,483 --> 00:19:27,103
Sparkle oars?

460
00:19:27,103 --> 00:19:28,123
Hey.

461
00:19:28,127 --> 00:19:29,127
Isn't that our boat?

462
00:19:29,127 --> 00:19:31,127
It is our boat!

463
00:19:31,127 --> 00:19:32,127
Hurry!

464
00:19:32,127 --> 00:19:33,127
Don't let it get away!

465
00:19:34,127 --> 00:19:36,127
Come back, boat!

466
00:19:37,127 --> 00:19:38,107
Whoa!

467
00:19:38,111 --> 00:19:40,111
Whoa!

468
00:19:44,111 --> 00:19:46,111
How did I get away?

469
00:19:46,111 --> 00:19:48,091
We tied up the boat, right mates?

470
00:19:48,095 --> 00:19:50,755
I thought you did it. I thought you did it.

471
00:19:50,755 --> 00:19:52,095
I guess no one did.

472
00:19:52,095 --> 00:19:53,435
Oops.

473
00:19:53,435 --> 00:19:55,635
It's okay. But the question is,

474
00:19:55,635 --> 00:19:58,075
how are we going to get home?

475
00:19:58,079 --> 00:20:00,079
We'll just think of a solution.

476
00:20:00,079 --> 00:20:02,079
Now everybody think.

477
00:20:06,079 --> 00:20:08,059
If only we could have a solution.

478
00:20:08,063 --> 00:20:09,723
- We had another boat.

479
00:20:09,723 --> 00:20:12,063
- It's not like they grow on trees.

480
00:20:13,443 --> 00:20:16,103
Wait, maybe they do.

481
00:20:16,103 --> 00:20:18,043
If we can find some long-bring

482
00:20:18,047 --> 00:20:20,047
Aye, aye, Captain!

483
00:20:28,031 --> 00:20:31,031
and tie them together, then.

484
00:20:32,031 --> 00:20:35,031
We can build a really impressive raft.

485
00:20:36,031 --> 00:20:38,011
All aboard!

486
00:20:38,015 --> 00:20:40,355
Word for home!

487
00:20:40,355 --> 00:20:44,015
Okay, grab the oars.

488
00:20:44,015 --> 00:20:47,995
- Might I point out the oars went off with our boat.

489
00:20:47,999 --> 00:20:49,399
So that's it then.

490
00:20:49,399 --> 00:20:52,579
We're stuck here, all of us, lost in the wilds.

491
00:20:52,579 --> 00:20:55,179
We'll never ever sleep in our comfy beds again.

492
00:20:55,179 --> 00:20:57,279
And I'll never have another story time with Oliver

493
00:20:57,279 --> 00:20:57,979
or another cookie.

494
00:20:57,983 --> 00:21:02,283
dipped in milk and our daring adventure is ruined forever.

495
00:21:02,283 --> 00:21:04,283
Oh.

496
00:21:04,283 --> 00:21:05,863
Don't worry, Captain.

497
00:21:05,863 --> 00:21:07,963
There's more than one way to solve a problem.

498
00:21:07,967 --> 00:21:10,007
- Wait a minute.

499
00:21:10,007 --> 00:21:11,307
The wind!

500
00:21:11,307 --> 00:21:15,307
We just need a sail so the wind can carry us across.

501
00:21:15,307 --> 00:21:17,947
Except, where's the wind?

502
00:21:17,951 --> 00:21:19,991
Where can we find a sail?

503
00:21:19,991 --> 00:21:21,711
How about our picnic blanket?

504
00:21:21,711 --> 00:21:22,711
Brilliant!

505
00:21:22,711 --> 00:21:24,411
A picnic blanket sail.

506
00:21:24,411 --> 00:21:25,711
Can you fix it up, Cat?

507
00:21:25,711 --> 00:21:27,931
Can I?

508
00:21:27,935 --> 00:21:31,935
Where's ship shape, Captain?

509
00:21:31,935 --> 00:21:33,935
To home!

510
00:21:33,935 --> 00:21:34,935
Oh!

511
00:21:34,935 --> 00:21:36,935
Woo-hoo-hoo!

512
00:21:36,935 --> 00:21:37,915
Oh!

513
00:21:37,919 --> 00:21:40,959
We did it! We rescued ourselves!

514
00:21:40,959 --> 00:21:43,959
Look! Isn't that Oliver?

515
00:21:43,959 --> 00:21:45,959
Look at that! He found our boat!

516
00:21:45,959 --> 00:21:47,899
Hey, Oliver! We're here!

517
00:21:47,903 --> 00:21:49,903
Over here! See?

518
00:21:49,903 --> 00:21:51,903
Whoa!

519
00:21:51,903 --> 00:21:55,903
I meant to stop doing that.

520
00:21:55,903 --> 00:21:57,883
You came on the adventure!

521
00:21:57,887 --> 00:21:59,187
You're the best.

522
00:21:59,287 --> 00:22:01,927
When I found the raft, I figured you needed help.

523
00:22:02,027 --> 00:22:05,367
But it looks like you figured it out all by yourselves.

524
00:22:05,467 --> 00:22:07,867
We put our minds to it and didn't give up.

525
00:22:07,871 --> 00:22:12,871
So, as my final act as captain,

526
00:22:12,871 --> 00:22:17,851
I'll just tie the raft to the shore.

527
00:22:17,855 --> 00:22:21,695
When your mouse is done with this daring adventure,

528
00:22:21,695 --> 00:22:23,395
there's a good chance he'll want--

529
00:22:23,395 --> 00:22:25,655
- Uh, Oliver? - Yes, Mouse?

530
00:22:25,655 --> 00:22:27,835
I could really use a bottle of bubble bath.

531
00:22:27,839 --> 00:22:31,839
And if I give you a bottle of bubble bath,

532
00:22:31,839 --> 00:22:37,819
what do you think will happen next?

533
00:22:37,823 --> 00:22:42,063
If you give a mouse a cookie, then it'll ask for a glass of milk.

534
00:22:42,223 --> 00:22:46,083
Then one thing will lead to another and you never know what's next.

535
00:22:46,623 --> 00:22:47,783
Let's go to an experiment.

536
00:22:47,807 --> 00:22:57,787
We'll see you next time.

537
00:22:57,791 --> 00:23:01,791
If you gave a mouse a cookie, what do you think will happen next?

538
00:23:07,863 --> 00:23:09,923
you
